 four-eyed  four-armed monster  surrounded by flames which you know  not the most human looking dude i've  ever seen this man  was an absolute force of nature though  and it took a large group of other  sorcerers banding together to fight at  their absolute best to take him down  however death was far from the end for  sukuna  because he had such a wealth of cursed  energy upon his death he transformed  into a curse himself  this is kind of interesting because  ghetto's goal is to eliminate normal  humans so that only sorcerers remain  this is because sorcerers have better  control over their cursed energy  and when they die they're less likely to  become curses themselves  so it's a little bit strange that one of  the people who debatably was the  strongest curse energy sorcerer in  history  excluding gojo and maybe a few other  cases would become a curse himself  regardless in order to contain this  powerful curse the 20 fingers which it  was divided between were sealed away as  cursed objects  however their power would continue to  grow over time and by the time that  yugi's story begins  the steels are beginning to weaken of  course the occult members would  completely unseal one finger and yuji  would go on to eat that  and with some of zukuno's energy now  being released the rest of the fingers  start to resonate and more rapidly draw  in the curses around them  by this point in the manga we've seen  yuji eat about 15  fingers meaning there are only a few  left however each time he does  tsukuna becomes all that much more  powerful within him and his takeovers  become harder and harder to suppress  i feel like i have to bring up the  elephant in the room when we talk about  sukuna's curse and his 20 fingers  and that is what happened to the rest of  his body is it the case that only the  fingers remain or is the rest of his  body out there somewhere as well just  waiting to be reunited with them  it's definitely something i'm super  curious about as the idea o