ble  we've only really seen two fights  involving sukuna that demonstrated  any real sense of struggle or effort  being exerted  firstly with his 10 second fight with  gojo at the start of the story  and here we see gojo treating tsukuna  the same way that sukuna treated jogo  even sitting on him at one point after  tsukun's attack  but again this is sukuna with one finger  and we don't really know how much he's  being limited in this state  of course if you ask gojo it's pretty  obvious who would win the fight though  even if sukuna was fully revived  and then we have his fight with maharaga  this wasn't exactly a close  fight however it did take some serious  thinking on sukuna's part maharaga is a  shikigami summoned by megumi and its key  strength is adaptability  basically if any attack hits him and  hurts him he will adapt to become more  or less immune to it going forward  to this sukna opens his domain and  unleashes a barrage of attacks on the  shikigami until it's  pretty much at its limits and before he  can begin healing  tsukuna launches a massive fireball to  eliminate the monster  so in general we can probably place  tsukuna in the top two  if not three strongest characters in the  series and the interesting part of this  is that despite this power  his abilities are very simple in a  series where characters can summon these  10  shadow shikigami or control robots  remotely or  be a panda it seems that the more simple  and easy to understand ability is  the more powerful it is toto can clap to  swap places gojo  can push and pull things and sukuna can  cut things  at the core of sukhna's abilities is  just that cutting  specifically he's able to do it in two  varieties though dismantle which is used  to cut  inanimate objects and cleave which takes  into account  the target's level of cursed energy and  toughness before slashing into them to  ensure that they can be destroyed in one  cut  these are more useful when combined with  his domain expansion 